From e6b98a3da72a5e956421ffa1a247837f7ceab2f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 06:15:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Lighten the Careers hero scrim so the background image
 actually shows

The Careers hero was inheriting the default .page-hero-video::before
scrim, which was tuned for a busier video source and pushes to ~100%
opacity by the bottom of the section -- against the new (already
fairly dark) careers-background.jpeg, that crushed nearly all of the
image to black. Gave it its own lighter, left-to-right gradient scrim
(same technique as the About page's override), so the chip/circuit
board photo is now clearly visible on the right while the heading
text on the left stays fully readable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SjcntVjf5Nr2bdomgFdfPu
---
 styles.css | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/styles.css b/styles.css
index 2055e6c..b9b1260 100644
--- a/styles.css
+++ b/styles.css
@@ -3135,6 +3135,14 @@ h3 {
     #0714261f 100%
   );
 }
+.page-hero-video--careers::before {
+  background: linear-gradient(
+    90deg,
+    #050e1fc4 0%,
+    #07142680 45%,
+    #07142633 100%
+  );
+}
 .page-hero-video::after {
   content: "";
   position: absolute;
-- 
